 "degenerate_complete": {
  "_comment": "QUARANTINE — COMPLETE verdicts whose recovered interface has no input or no output. A module with nothing coming in, or nothing going out, cannot be written from that interface, so COMPLETE is false there whatever the count says. MAY ONLY SHRINK; the target is 0. An entry is a FINDING AWAITING ITS AUTHOR, not a dispensation: it is paid by repairing the reader chain so the record stops being degenerate, and the row is then deleted. Deleting a row on its own does not pay it — the test recomputes the set every run and an entry that comes back is a stale record, reported as its own failure. A NEW entry is a new false COMPLETE and blocks. This floor exists because a bare count cannot tell recovery-improvement from recovery-regression: 226->233 was both at once.",
  "ids": {
   "cvdp_copilot_gcd_0001": "0 inputs. Recovered interface is {controlpath_state}, which reads as FSM prose, not a port of the module input.prompt names (`gcd_top`, with clk/rst/go/A/B/OUT/done). Arrived with 11bb1cde7.",
   "cvdp_copilot_sequencial_binary_to_one_hot_decoder_0001": "0 outputs. Recovered interface is {i_clk, i_rstb}. input.prompt declares both data ports under '## Inputs and Outputs' WITH widths — `i_binary_in` (BINARY_WIDTH bits, Default 5) and `o_one_hot_out` (OUTPUT_WIDTH bits, Default 32) — over parameters the reader already recognises. Prompt-stated and missed: honest verdict is INCOMPLETE_EXTRACTION_GAP. Arrived with 11bb1cde7.",
   "cvdp_copilot_sigma_delta_audio_0007": "0 outputs. Recovered interface is 4 inputs, no output. PRE-EXISTING — degenerate on the fe27b28b7 arm too, so it is not a regression of 11bb1cde7 and is the reason this floor starts at 3 rather than 2."
